  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts` for the low-poly island scene, and it passes `typecheck`. I haven't run it in a browser and haven't run `vite build`, so the visuals and the animation are untested.\n\n- **Island:** A flat-shaded terrain mesh generated from code, with jittered vertices and a colour per face. Colours run sand, grass, rock and snow by height, and steep faces turn rocky. About 22 trees (two stacked cones on a trunk) and 14 rocks sit on it, all as instanced primitives. No model files.\n- **Water:** A large animated custom-shader plane with vertex waves, a fresnel sky reflection, a sun/moon glint, shallow-to-deep colour, and shoreline foam that moves. Its lighting and colours are updated every frame from the sun and sky.\n- **Day/night:** One full cycle takes 20 seconds, starting at 9:00.\n  - The Preetham sky sun, the directional sun with shadows, and a moon light all move each frame.\n  - The sun's colour shifts toward orange at dusk, and the hemisphere light and fog colour change with the time of day.\n  - Light intensities keep a floor (the moon and hemisphere light never fall to zero), so the scene is never black.\n- **Camera:** It sits 18 units above the water and orbits the island slowly at a distance of 40.\n- **Ready flag:** The render loop is the engine's own. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set to true one animation frame after `app.ready()` resolves.\n\nI used the shared `app.atmosphere.setSky` and `setFog` calls for the sky and fog, but I haven't confirmed they update every frame in the browser.\n\n",
